2. USER PROFILE — JOB SEEKER
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

All profile changes go through a single endpoint. Recruiters see this profile
when reviewing applications.

API:  PUT /api/users/me/profile
Page: /profile

2.1  Basic Information
     - Headline (e.g. "Frontend Engineer | React, TypeScript")
     - Location
     - Phone number
     - Bio / About
     - LinkedIn URL (auto-prefixed with https://)
     - Portfolio URL (auto-prefixed with https://)

2.2  Skills
     Comma-separated input. Max 20 skills, each up to 40 characters.

2.3  Avatar (Profile Photo)
     Upload JPG/PNG image, max 2 MB, stored as base64 data-URL.
     Circular 80×80 preview with remove option.

2.4  Education (Repeater)
     Dynamic list of education entries. Max 10 entries.
     Each entry: School, Degree, Field of Study, Start Year, End Year, Grade.

2.5  Work Experience (Repeater)
     Dynamic list of work entries. Max 10 entries.
     Each entry: Company, Title, Start Date, End Date, "Currently work here"
     checkbox (disables end date), Description.

2.6  Certifications (Repeater)
     Dynamic list. Max 10 entries.
     Each entry: Name, Issuer, Date, URL.

2.7  Languages (Repeater)
     Dynamic list. Max 10 entries.
     Each entry: Language, Proficiency (Elementary → Native).

2.8  Job Preferences
     - Preferred job types: Full-time, Part-time, Contract, Internship (checkboxes)
     - Preferred work modes: On-site, Remote, Hybrid (checkboxes)
     - Expected salary range (min/max)
     - Preferred locations (comma-separated)

2.9  Resume Management
     Upload: PDF, DOC, DOCX, or TXT. Max 2 MB. Stored as base64 data-URL.
     Download: One-click download via <a download>.
     Remove: Delete resume from profile.
     API:  POST /api/users/me/resume
           DELETE /api/users/me/resume
     Page: /profile (Resume section)

2.10 Profile Save & Context Sync
     After saving, the updated user is set directly in React Context from
     the API response (no reliance on a second refresh call). Ensures
     canApply guard and other checks see the latest profile immediately.
     User stays on /profile after save (no redirect away).


