4. COMPANY MANAGEMENT
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

4.1  Register Company
     Recruiter creates company profile with all details below.
     This is Step 2 of the onboarding flow (after email verification).
     Also sets users.company on the recruiter's user record.
     API:  POST /api/companies
     Page: /register-company

     Fields:
     - Company name *
     - Location *
     - Industry type * (Technology, Finance, Healthcare, Education, Marketing,
       Design, Consulting, Manufacturing, Retail, Other)
     - Company size (1-10, 11-50, 51-200, 201-500, 501-1000, 1000+)
     - Website URL
     - Description *
     - Logo (circular image, max 2 MB, stored as base64 data-URL)
     - Founded year (1900 – current year)
     - Social links (LinkedIn, Twitter/X, Facebook, Instagram)
     - Tech stack (tag input, max 30 items — React, Node.js, PostgreSQL, etc.)
     - Benefits (checkbox grid: Health insurance, Flexible hours, Remote work,
       Paid time off, Learning budget, 401k/EPF, Free meals, Team outings,
       Stock options)
     - Culture (free text, max 3000 chars)
     - Company status * (Registered / Unregistered — self-declared radio toggle,
       defaults to Unregistered)

4.2  Edit Company
     Update all company fields. Only the owning recruiter can edit.
     API:  PUT /api/companies/:id
     Page: /edit-company

4.3  View Company Profile (Public)
     Full public page showing all company details, open positions, team members.
     API:  GET /api/companies/:id
     Page: /company/:id

     Sections:
     - Logo (64px) aligned with name + registered badge (flex row)
     - Location, industry, size, founded year (indented to match logo width)
     - Website link, social links
     - Description
     - Tech stack tags
     - Benefits tags
     - Culture text
     - Open Positions (list of active jobs)
     - Team on Board (shortlisted/accepted candidates with avatars)

4.4  Browse Companies (Directory)
     Paginated, searchable directory of all companies.
     Search by name, location, or industry. 250ms debounce.
     Fixed-height cards: descriptions truncated at 60px via CSS overflow.
     Clicking "Show more" button (below the truncated text) expands the card.
     Each card shows: logo + name, job count, registered badge, location,
     industry, size, truncated description with "Show more/less" toggle.
     API:  GET /api/companies?page=&limit=&q=
     Page: /companies

4.5  Get My Company
     Fetch the logged-in recruiter's registered company.
     API:  GET /api/companies/mine
     File: context/AuthContext.jsx (auto-fetches on mount for recruiters)


