5. JOB POSTING — RECRUITER
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Prerequisites: email verified + registered company + profile headline set.

5.1  Create Job Posting
     API:  POST /api/jobs
     Page: /post

     Fields:
     - Job title *
     - Company (auto-filled from registered company, shown as static text)
     - Location *
     - Job type (Full-time, Part-time, Internship, Contract)
     - Work mode (On-site, Remote, Hybrid)
     - Experience level (Internship, Entry level, Associate, Mid-Senior level,
       Director, Executive)
     - Salary range (min, max, currency: INR/USD/EUR/GBP)
     - Openings (1–999)
     - Application deadline (future date)
     - Description *
     - Requirements
     - Required skills (tag input, max 20 items)
     - Benefits (checkbox grid, same 9 options as company)

5.2  Edit Job Posting
     Pre-fills all fields from existing job. Accessed via URL param ?id=.
     API:  PUT /api/jobs/:id
     Page: /post?id=X

5.3  Toggle Job Active/Inactive
     Close or reopen a job. Closed jobs don't appear in search and don't
     accept applications.
     API:  PATCH /api/jobs/:id/toggle-active
     Page: MyJobs.jsx (button per job)

5.4  Delete Job Posting
     Permanently deletes job, all applications, related conversations/messages,
     and application notifications. Confirmation modal shows applicant count.
     API:  DELETE /api/jobs/:id
     Page: MyJobs.jsx (button → confirmation modal)

5.5  My Postings Dashboard
     Lists all jobs posted by the recruiter. Each card shows:
     - Title, company logo + name (link to profile), registered badge
     - Tags: closed badge (if inactive), job type (dark), salary (dark)
     - Applicant count
     - Actions: View applicants, Edit, Close/Reopen, Delete
     API:  GET /api/jobs/mine
     Page: /my-jobs

5.6  Job Expiration
     Jobs stop accepting applications after their expires_at date.
     Soft-close: job remains visible but shows "Applications closed" badge.
     Company can still see all applicants on closed/expired jobs.
     Companies cannot see job IDs on expired listings.


