6. JOB BROWSING & APPLICATION — JOB SEEKER
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

6.1  Browse Jobs
     Paginated, searchable list of active jobs.
     Search by title, company, or location. 250ms debounce.
     Applied jobs are automatically hidden from the browse list (filtered
     client-side via myAppliedJobIds API). Only non-applied jobs are shown.
     Each job card shows:
     - Title (link to detail), company logo + name (link to profile), location
     - Registered/Unregistered badge (right side)
     - Tags: job type (dark), salary range (dark)
     - Posted date, openings count
     - Expiration: "Applications closed" (red) / "Closing soon" (amber, <3 days)
     - "Apply now" button
     API:  GET /api/jobs?q=&page=&limit=
           GET /api/jobs/mine/applied  (returns applied job IDs for filtering)
     Page: /browse (requires login)

6.2  Job Detail Page
     Full job view with back button, all tags, dates, description, requirements,
     "About the company" summary card (with company logo, name, registered
     badge, and "View company profile" link), "Team on Board" section
     (with member avatars), apply/status.
     API:  GET /api/jobs/:id
           GET /api/jobs/company/:companyId/team
     Page: /jobs/:id

6.3  Apply to Job (Modal)
     Application form with:
     - Name (pre-filled from profile)
     - Email (pre-filled)
     - Phone (pre-filled from profile)
     - Portfolio URL
     - Expected salary
     - Cover note (optional, max 2000 chars)
     Client-side guard: must be logged in, must be seeker, must have verified
     email, must have headline + skills.
     API:  POST /api/jobs/:id/apply
     Component: ApplyModal.jsx

6.4  My Applications Dashboard
     Lists all jobs the seeker has applied to. Each row shows:
     - Job title (or "Deleted posting")
     - Company link + location
     - Applied date
     - Status badge (color-coded)
     - "Message recruiter" button (if shortlisted/accepted)
     API:  GET /api/jobs/applications/mine
     Page: /applications

6.5  Application Status Labels
     Color-coded badges: applied (blue), in-review (yellow),
     shortlisted (green), rejected (red), accepted (purple).
     File: status.js — statusLabel(), statusClass()


