7. APPLICANT MANAGEMENT — RECRUITER
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

7.1  View Applicants
     Expandable list for each job showing:
     - Avatar (or initial fallback) + name, email, phone, portfolio link,
       expected salary, cover note, application date
     - Status dropdown, "View profile" button, "Message" button
     API:  GET /api/jobs/:id/applicants
     Page: MyJobs.jsx (toggle per job)

7.2  Update Application Status
     Change status: applied → in-review → shortlisted / rejected / accepted.
     Status changes trigger notifications to the seeker.
     Accepting auto-assigns the seeker to the company.
     API:  PATCH /api/jobs/:jobId/applicants/:appId
     Page: MyJobs.jsx (dropdown per applicant)

7.3  View Seeker Profile (Modal)
     Full profile modal showing all seeker data + application-specific data
     (phone, portfolio, expected salary). Includes resume download.
     Page: MyJobs.jsx → "View profile" button

7.4  Notifications on Apply
     When a seeker applies, the recruiter gets: "{name} applied to "{title}""
     (type: application, links to /my-jobs).

7.5  Notifications on Status Change
     When status changes, seeker gets: "Your application for "{title}" is now
     {status}" (type: application-status, links to /applications).


