9. MESSAGING
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Messaging is only allowed between a recruiter and seeker when the seeker's
application status is "shortlisted" or "accepted" for a specific job.

9.1  Conversations List
     Sidebar showing all conversations sorted by last message time.
     Each shows: other person's avatar (or initial fallback), name, job title,
     company, last message preview, timestamp, unread count badge.
     API:  GET /api/messages/conversations

9.2  Open Thread
     Click a conversation to open it. Shows full message history with timestamps.
     API:  GET /api/messages/:id

9.3  Open Thread by Job + Person
     "Message recruiter" / "Message" buttons navigate to:
     /messages?job=X&with=Y — auto-opens or creates the conversation.
     API:  GET /api/messages/thread?jobId=&with=

9.4  Send Message
     Text input + "Send" button. Max 5000 chars per message.
     Auto-creates conversation if it doesn't exist.
     API:  POST /api/messages

9.5  Auto-Refresh
     Messages and conversation list poll every 5 seconds while viewing a thread.

9.6  Unread Count
     Badge in conversation list header shows total unread messages.

9.7  Mark as Read
     Messages are automatically marked as read when opening a conversation.

9.8  Notification on New Message
     Recipient gets: "New message from {name}" (type: message).

9.9  Responsive Layout
     Mobile: toggles between conversation list and thread view.
     "Back" button returns to list.

9.10 Message Timestamps
     Shows time (HH:MM) for same-day messages, date otherwise.

9.11 Auto-Scroll
     Thread auto-scrolls to the latest message on new messages.


